      "sections": [
        {
          "heading": "Introduction and notation",
          "body": "The Sylow theorems are the first structural results about finite groups beyond Lagrange's theorem. We give self-contained proofs of existence (Sylow I), conjugacy (Sylow II) and the counting conditions (Sylow III), together with the index formula for the normalizer and the uniqueness criterion. Notation is fixed in Section 2; all results are stated and proved in Section 3; examples and references follow."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Definitions and notation",
          "body": "|G| order; p-Sylow subgroup = subgroup of order p^k where p^k is the full p-part of |G|; N_G(H) normalizer; orbit-stabilizer; class equation; fixed-point congruence for p-groups."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Main results",
          "body": "Theorem 3.1 (Sylow I): existence and containment. Theorem 3.2 (Sylow II): conjugacy. Theorem 3.3 (Sylow III): n_p | m and n_p = 1 (mod p). Theorem 3.4: n_p = [G : N_G(P)]. Theorem 3.5: uniqueness iff normality."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Examples and comparison with the literature",
          "body": "S_3, S_4, A_5 and groups of order pq illustrate the counting conditions; the treatment follows the expository accounts of the reference list."
        }
      ],
